# Standard `.clro` Note

`.clro` is the application's default note format. It supports Markdown plus helper markup for underline, color, background color, and internal-note markers.

## Study checklist

- [x] Read a heading
- [ ] Edit this item
- Note: `inline_code`
- [ ] Try `Save > Save Work`

**bold**, *italic*, ~~strikethrough~~, and `code-style text`

> Start a quotation with `>`. Use the helper markup below only where ordinary Markdown is not enough.

<u>underlined text</>

<char=1a73e8>blue text</>

<back=fff2cc>text with a background color</>

<font="Segoe UI"><size=15>text with an explicit font and size</></>

## PDF round-trip link

<link=session-02-pdf-note-link><la><lu>Open the PDF link-practice marker</></></>

Click the link above to move to the blue annotation marker in `pdf_link_practice.pdf` in this folder. Click the blue annotation marker in the PDF to return to this location in the note. The same-named `.clrop` is application-managed data that stores this association, so keep it with the PDF.

| Item | Example | Status |
| :--- | :---: | ---: |
| Markdown | headings and lists | checked |
| Helper markup | underline, color, links | editable |

Math also works: \(a^2 + b^2 = c^2\)
